- * C: is the cartridge's save RAM, and on a Mode 1 boot the flash cart
- * writes it to an SD card by itself. That closes the loop: hold Down,
- * read the log off the card. It used to take a second boot into a
- * different ROM -- boot/m1tool.S existed to copy B: across -- and
- * before that a CD-R per question.
- *
- * B: is the fallback and used to be the only choice: 8 KB of internal
- * backup RAM on the sub CPU's own bus. EmuTOS will not touch it while
- * it holds Sega-format game saves, so the log had nowhere to go until
- * C was held at power-on once to claim it. On a CD boot with no
- * cartridge fitted, C: is the disc, Fcreate fails on it because it is
